Gas energy ledger for GIZMO (diagnostic only; not meant for the main line).

Books every change of gas kinetic energy (relative to the shear flow in shearing boxes) and
thermal energy to a channel, and checks the books at each full synchronization:

    git apply scripts/energy_ledger.patch          # or git apply -3
    # Config: ENERGY_LEDGER                        (optional: LEDGER_TRACE_ID=<particle ID>)

OUTPUT (OutputDir):
  energy_ledger.txt     one line per full sync: time, E_kin, E_th, dE, residual (dE minus all
                        channels; roundoff when the books close), then the channels in the order of
                        the LG_* enum in core/proto.h -- hydro work W, hydro heat Q, hydro limiter,
                        gravity (incl. Coriolis/tidal), shear drift, long-range RP, turbulence,
                        feedback KE/TE applied, local RP, HII heating, HII recombination, radiative
                        gain/loss, floors, SF removal, outflow, merge/split, then (not part of the
                        closure) feedback energy intended and feedback energy deferred to the hydro du.
  ledger_events_<task>.txt   single-cell hydro events with |dQ+dW| > 0.05e51 erg (pc/Msun/km/s
                        units), with the cell's state, timestep and bin.
  ledger_trace_<task>.txt    with LEDGER_TRACE_ID: every kick, wake check and wakeup of that cell.

HOW TO READ IT: in an MFM run hydro W+Q over any window should be ~0 (hydro exchanges energy, it
does not create it). Compare W+Q against the feedback energy applied in the same window. In the
FIRE-3 tall box (scripts/tallbox) at 10-100 Msun, W+Q reaches 2-12x the SN energy input, from
cells on long timesteps that receive no warning of a nearby SN: the closing half-kick applies
the post-SN hydro force over the whole half-step.

One MPI_Reduce per full sync. Tested with the tall-box config only; booking sites outside the
physics it enables (other cooling paths, RT, CRs, sinks) are absent.
