 #PARTICLE_MERGE_SPLIT_EVERY_TIMESTEP     # force merge/split operations to occur every timestep, instead of only on domain decomposition steps
 #MHD_CONSERVE_B_ON_REFINEMENT      # redefine B after density step after a refinement/de-refinement operation so as to exactly conserve "B" between the steps, as compared to conserving the code "VB" between the steps [the default conserved integrated quantity]
+#ENERGY_LEDGER                     # gas energy ledger, no behaviour change: every operation that changes gas kinetic (relative to the shear flow in shearing boxes) or thermal energy books it to a channel -- hydro work and heat, gravity (incl. shearing-box Coriolis + tidal), shear drift, radiation pressure, mechanical feedback (applied and intended), HII heating, radiative gain/loss, floors and limiters, star formation, outflow, merge/split. At each full synchronization energy_ledger.txt gets E_kin, E_th, their change, every channel, and the residual (change minus the channels): any unbooked change, or hydro W+Q != 0, flags non-conservation. One MPI_Reduce per synchronization.
 #ENERGY_BUDGET_DIAGNOSTIC           # energy diagnostics, no behaviour change. Reports (a) the total gas energy (thermal+kinetic) at every full synchronization, i.e. when All.HighestActiveTimeBin == All.HighestOccupiedTimeBin -- the only point at which Vel and InternalEnergy share a clock and the sum is a genuine conserved quantity, so the 'Energy (synced)' line is the real conservation test and in an adiabatic run should track the injected energy exactly (its E_fb field is the cumulative energy mechanical feedback has written into the gas, to compare against); and (b) cumulative wakeup tallies from timestep.cc -- the residual left by the kick reversal, and processed wakeups split by trigger (hydro / merge / split / newly-spawned) and demotion depth. Do NOT substitute snapshots for the synced total: io.cc writes Velocities from P[].Vel (kick-time) but InternalEnergy from InternalEnergyPred (drift-time), so a snapshot sum is mixed-clock and not conserved. Costs one MPI_Allreduce per synchronization. The per-phase breakdown that once accompanied this (kick1/drift/grav/hydro/mergesplit/kick2/spawn/srcterms, one Allreduce per mark) was hoisted out to scripts/energy_budget_phases.patch -- apply that to localize an error to a specific stage of the step.
 #  MERGE_SPLIT_ENERGY_DIAGNOSTIC was hoisted out to scripts/merge_energy_diagnostic.patch -- apply that to get it back; setting the flag alone does nothing. It reports the cumulative energy budget of merge operations: dE (change in the true InternalEnergy+KE), dE_pred (same for the predicted variables the hydro actually integrates), KE_com (what a momentum-conserving merge must dissipate), resid (the correction merge_particles_ij computes), how often the InternalEnergyPred floor fires, and the TimeBin/Ti_current relationship of merged pairs. The patch header records what it established, including the dead ends worth not repeating.
 #SNE_BROADCAST_TIMESTEP            # FIRE mechanical SNe without energy creation from long gas timesteps; no parameters. Feedback is deposited after the closing kick (steps ending now close with pre-SN forces), SN heat goes in instantly rather than as a deferred du/dt, and recipients choose their next step from their post-injection signal speed (Durier & Dalla Vecchia 2012). Each SN reaches gas at distance r no sooner than r/v, v = min(v_ejecta, sqrt(2 E_SN / m_gas)): every gas cell caps its next step at 0.5 CourantFac r/v, and one whose current step would outlast that is woken now. Without it, a cell on a long step gets the post-SN pressure force over its whole closing half-kick and creates energy (several x E_SN in test/sn_cluster_adiabatic and the FIRE tall box at 10-100 Msun). Costs one Allgather and a loop over local gas on steps with SNe.
